{"schema_version":"1","verdict":"ACCEPT","verdict_reason":"The six F62 fixes match the remedies, and the remaining parser and no-hard-link limits do not reopen those defects.","reply_markdown":"## 1. F62-1\n\nNo comparison in `maintain/` still treats equal numbers as the same release. `parts` is private and used only inside `precedence` (`crates/c3/src/maintain/version.rs:70`). Attribution uses `same_release` (`crates/c3/src/maintain/mod.rs:1048`, `1076`, `1212`, `1232`, `1255`, `1290`). \"Newer\" uses `is_newer_than` (`mod.rs:906`, `1364`).\n\nThe parser keeps the tag and build metadata (`version.rs:183`). `1.0.80-rc.1`, `1.0.80rc1`, and `1.0.80+build.7` stay distinct from `1.0.80`, and tag case is kept. It collapses a leading `v`/`V`, a trailing `.`, and a suffix of only ASCII punctuation (`version.rs:136`, `192`). `1.0` and `1.0.0` stay different identities and tie in ordering, so neither is installed over the other. A dotted token whose component does not fit in `u64` is `Token::Other`, and the scan continues (`version.rs:175`, `140`); the comment at `version.rs:131` says that scan stops. No recorded CLI version has such a component.\n\nExact identity does not break the recorded updaters. Codex is npm: `npm view … version` and `codex-cli 0.169.0` parse to one token (`engine.rs:5`, `135`; `version.rs:406`). Grok pins `latestVersion`; `--version` is `grok 1.0.77 (hash) [stable]` (`engine.rs:10`, `193`). Kimi is the vendor installer with `KIMI_VERSION`, which is the parsed marker (`engine.rs:13`, `337`). Agy has no check and no pin (`engine.rs:16`, `114`). A `--version` that adds build metadata the vendor string lacks would be \"did not take\"; these shapes have none. Real binaries were not run.\n\n## 2. F62-3\n\n`published_from` is the only publisher (`models.rs:1041`). It keeps an id only when `provenance` returns a key that today's `trusted_sources` still lists (`models.rs:1044`). `provenance` requires `SourceList.public` and, for a catalog, `web:` plus the canonical `url` equal to the record name (`web.rs:170`). A disagreeing url yields `None` (`web.rs:172`). A legacy custom catalog or page with no `url` and no `public` yields `None` (`web.rs:174`). The exception is a status-less name that is exactly a `DEFAULT_CATALOGS` URL (`web.rs:180`): the built-in OpenRouter catalog, which excludes another URL on that host and `web:openrouter.ai`. Collect writes `url` and `public` for both kinds (`web.rs:361`). The new reclassification tests lock the private-then-public cache. Rows that only add `public: true` on an already-trusted catalog do not, by themselves, fail if that gate is removed.\n\n## 3. F62-2, F62-4, F62-5, F62-6, no exchange\n\nF62-2: `resolve_collab_root_with` collapses `.` and `..` by text before the link check and `canonicalize` (`providers.rs:2569`). Consult, panel, and detach use it. `c3 work` already did (`work/mod.rs:203`). The checked directory and the written directory are that textual path.\n\nF62-4: the displaced name is taken by `hard_link`, which fails when the name exists, then `-2`, `-3` (`contain.rs:861`). The millisecond overwrite and the unchecked suffix 1000 are closed. With no hard links, or after 1000 taken names, a 32-hex name is checked and then `rename`d (`contain.rs:873`). That step can still replace a name created in the gap. It does not reuse the timestamp name.\n\nF62-5: once the parent is `collaboration`, recursion keeps that name at every depth (`quota.rs:1113`). A nested function or hosted tool is a breach. The same nesting outside it stays a complete list.\n\nF62-6: `bounded_stem` cuts at 120 bytes on a character boundary (`reviewed.rs:785`). The long names are stem+104 and stem+102 (`reviewed.rs:776`), so 224 and 222 bytes. The digest stays whole, so two briefs that share a 120-byte prefix stay different files. The cut can land mid-slug; that is the remedy.\n\n`publish_exchange` refuses when there is no atomic exchange (`contain.rs:725`). Callers are the roster write (`models.rs:1219`) and agent repair (`repo_models.rs:517`); both return the error. `Publication::Rename` is gone. A missing file is created by hard link; if that link cannot be made, the create is refused too (`contain.rs:769`).\n\n## 4. Tests\n\nThese fail without their fix: the three maintain recovery/update tests, both catalog reclassification tests, `two_displaced_versions_never_share_a_name_and_nothing_is_replaced`, the quota ancestry test, `a_long_brief_stem_is_bounded_so_every_patch_name_fits`, the refusal assertions before the hook is dropped, and `resolve_collab_root` in `state_dir/tests.rs` where `canonicalize` follows the symlink.\n\nThese do not: `work.rs` `a_collab_path_with_dot_dot_after_a_link_is_taken_by_text` only runs `c3 work`, already lexical before this commit. The `first.txt` write in the no-exchange test runs after `drop(_off)` (`contain.rs:2015`). `a_published_claude_id_spelled_with_dots_is_sent_by_its_dash_name` only adds `url`/`public` on the built-in catalog; a status-less built-in record is still published.\n\nNot read: `update/` self-update, the `ReplaceFileW` body past its error map, and c3-cli suites other than these hunks. Nothing was executed.\n","findings":[{"severity":"note","locations":[{"path":"crates/c3/src/maintain/version.rs","line":175},{"path":"crates/c3/src/maintain/version.rs","line":140},{"path":"crates/c3/src/maintain/version.rs","line":131}],"claim":"A dotted token whose numeric component does not fit in u64 is classified as not version-shaped, so parse_cli_version keeps scanning and can return a later token. The comment says the first version-shaped token that cannot be read exactly ends the scan.","trigger":"A --version line whose first major.minor token contains a component greater than u64::MAX, followed by another version token.","evidence":[{"kind":"read-code","reference":"crates/c3/src/maintain/version.rs:169-176","observation":"A failed u64 parse of the digit-and-dot prefix returns Token::Other."},{"kind":"read-code","reference":"crates/c3/src/maintain/version.rs:134-141","observation":"Token::Other continues the loop; only Token::Unclear returns None. The comment at lines 131-133 says a later number is not taken."}],"verification":"Call parse_cli_version on \"tool 18446744073709551616.1 also 1.2.3\" and expect None under the stated rule.","remedy":"When the digit-and-dot prefix has at least two components and any component fails to parse as u64, return Token::Unclear.","supersedes":[]}],"prior_findings":[{"id":"F02-1","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-2","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-3","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-4","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-5","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-6","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-7","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-8","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-9","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-10","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-11","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-12","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-13","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F02-14","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only.