:"F51-6","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F52-1","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F52-2","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F52-4","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F53-1","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F53-2","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F53-3","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F53-4","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F53-5","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F53-6","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F53-7","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-1","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-2","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-3","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-4","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-5","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-6","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-7","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-8","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-9","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F57-10","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F60-1","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F60-2","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F60-3","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F61-1","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F61-3","status":"not-checked","note":"Not re-audited; this review covered the F62 fix commit only."},{"id":"F62-1","status":"fixed","note":"Recovery and post-update checks use same_release; ordering uses is_newer_than. 1.0.80-rc.1 is not 1.0{"schema_version":"1","verdict":"ACCEPT","verdict_reason":"The six F62 remedies hold in the changed code, and the one parser residual does not treat a pre-release as its final release.","reply_markdown":"## 1. F62-1\n\n`maintain/` decides \"same release\" only with `same_release` (`version.rs:61`). `parts` is private and feeds `precedence` alone (`version.rs:70`). Call sites: `mod.rs:1048`, `1076`, `1212`, `1232`, `1255`, `1290`. \"Newer\" is `is_newer_than` (`mod.rs:906`, `1364`).\n\nKept in the identity: tag and build metadata (`version.rs:200`). Dropped: a leading `v`/`V`, a trailing `.`, and an ASCII-punctuation suffix (`version.rs:136`, `192`). `1.0.80-rc.1`, `1.0.80rc1`, `1.0.80+build.7` and `1.0.80-RC.1` are not `1.0.80` and not each other. `1.0` and `1.0.0` tie in order and differ as identities, so neither is installed over the other nor verifies it. `1.0.80(rc1)` and `1.0.80_rc1` stop the scan (`version.rs:139`). A component above `u64::MAX` is `Other` (`version.rs:175`) and a later token is still read (finding #1). That path does not treat a pre-release as its final release.\n\nRecorded updaters still round-trip (`engine.rs:4`). Codex pairs the npm version text with `codex-cli <version>`. Grok pairs `latestVersion` with `grok <version> (hash) [stable]`. Kimi is the vendor installer pinned by `KIMI_VERSION` (`engine.rs:298`), not npm. Agy has no check and no pin (`engine.rs:16`). Build metadata present on only one side would fail the exact check; those shapes have none.\n\n## 2. F62-3\n\nOnly `published_from` (`models.rs:1041`) publishes. It keeps an id only when `provenance` (`web.rs:162`) matches a key trusted now (`models.rs:1044`). A catalog key requires `public` and the canonical `url` equal to the record name (`web.rs:170`). A mismatched url/name, a legacy custom catalog, and a label-only page publish nothing. The legacy exception is an empty `url` whose name is exactly a built-in catalog URL (`web.rs:174`, `web.rs:180`). Collect writes `url` and `public` together (`web.rs:361`). The new private-cache assertions fail on the old function. Fixtures that only add `\"public\":true` on an already-trusted URL do not make those assertions pass.\n\n## 3. F62-2, F62-4, F62-5, F62-6, refusal\n\nF62-2. `lexical` runs before the link check and `canonicalize` (`providers.rs:2569`). Consult, panel and detach share it. `c3 work` already did (`work/mod.rs:203`).\n\nF62-4. `hard_link` takes `stem`, then `-2` upward (`contain.rs:861`), so an occupied thousandth name is not returned unchecked. Without hard links, a 32-hex suffix is checked and renamed (`contain.rs:873`); that gap can still replace a name created in between, and it does not reuse the millisecond name. Unsupported exchange, and a missing file that cannot be hard-linked, are refused (`contain.rs:726`, `769`). `models.rs:1219` and `repo_models.rs:517` return the error. `Publication::Rename` is gone.\n\nF62-5. Inside `collaboration`, the child walk keeps that name (`quota.rs:1113`). Nested functions and hosted tools are breaches. The same nesting outside stays complete.\n\nF62-6. `bounded_stem` (`reviewed.rs:785`) cuts to 120 bytes on a character boundary. Names add at most 104 bytes (`reviewed.rs:777`), 224 ≤ 255. The digest is whole. A slug can be split; a shared prefix still differs by digest.\n\n## 4. Tests\n\nThe new `work.rs` dot-dot test stays green if `providers.rs:2569` is reverted, because `c3 work` already called `lexical`. `state_dir/tests.rs` locks `resolve_collab_root` where canonicalize follows the link. The first-write block after `drop(_off)` (`contain.rs:2015`) stays green if the refusal is reverted; the refusal assertions above it do not. Built-in-catalog fixtures that only gained `\"public\":true` stay green if the flag is ignored. The new \"cached while private\" tests do not.\n\nNot executed: the tests and live `--version` strings. Findings before F62 were not re-audited.","findings":[{"severity":"minor","locations":[{"path":"crates/c3/src/maintain/version.rs","line":175},{"path":"crates/c3/src/maintain/version.rs","line":140}],"claim":"A version-shaped token whose numeric component does not fit in u64 is classified as Other, so parse_cli_version keeps scanning and can return a later version token. The comment says the first version-shaped token that cannot be read exactly stops the scan.","trigger":"A --version line whose first dotted token contains a component greater than u64::MAX, followed by another version token.","evidence":[{"kind":"read-code","reference":"crates/c3/src/maintain/version.rs:169-176 and :134-141","observation":"read_token returns Token::Other when u64 parsing of a digit-and-dot head fails. parse_cli_version continues on Other and returns None only on Unclear."}],"verification":"Call parse_cli_version on a string whose first token is 1.<2^64>.0 and whose second token is 9.9.9, and check whether the result is None or 9.9.9.","remedy":"Return Token::Unclear when a digit-and-dot token has at least two components and one of them does not parse as u64.","supersedes":[]}],"prior_findings":[{"id":"F02-1","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-2","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-3","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-4","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-5","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-6","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-7","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-8","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-9","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-10","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-11","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-12","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-13","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-14","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-15","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-16","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-17","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-18","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-19","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-20","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F02-21","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F03-1","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F03-2","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in this commit; not re-audited."},{"id":"F03-3","status":"not-checked","note":"Not in thi